imation (from constraint 2). Thus, position 1 must watch thriller (since the genres are unique).\n4. Now assign jobs. We know position 1 is a videographer (from constraint 2), so position 2 must be a freelancer (since jobs are unique).\n5. Check nationalities: position 2 is pakistani, so position 1 must be nigerian. This matches the uniqueness constraint.\n\n### Final assignments:\n- Position 1:\n  - Job: videographer\n  - Movie-Genre: thriller\n  - Nationality: nigerian\n\n- Position 2:\n  - Job: freelancer\n  - Movie-Genre: animation\n  - Nationality: pakistani\n\n### Answering the questions:\n1. What is the job of the person who is pakistani?\n   -> Position 2 is pakistani and their job is freelancer.\n\n2. What is the movie genre of the person who is pakistani?\n   -> Position 2 is pakistani and their movie-genre is animation.\n\n3. What movie genre does the person in position 1 watch?\n   -> Position 1 watches thriller.\n\n4. At what position is the person who is a videographer?\n   -> The videographer is in position 1.\n\n### Final ordered answers:\n<solution>freelancer, animation, thriller, 1</solution>\n\nFinal answer: <solution>freelancer, animation, thriller, 1</solution>", "logprobs": [{"token": "Let", "logprob": -0.29888519644737244}, {"token": "'s", "logprob": -0.024908771738409996}, {"token": " break", "logprob": -1.0404311418533325}, {"token": " down", "logprob": -0.20462356507778168}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.022575635462999344}, {"token": " problem", "logprob": -0.07506551593542099}, {"token": " step", "logprob": -0.102035753428936}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -0.06998813897371292}, {"token": " step", "logprob": -0.0010372978867962956}, {"token": " using", "logprob": -1.4535152912139893}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.10976191610097885}, {"token": " given", "logprob": -0.32242169976234436}, {"token": " information", "logprob": -1.4676876068115234}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -1.1830893754959106}, {"token": " constraints", "logprob": -0.2